||false|false&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Copyright \u00a9 2020\u00a0Westside Pacific Villages |\u00a0Website by <a href=\"http:\/\/seanstory.com\/\">Spotlight Story Productions, LLC.<\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_text][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>[et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; disabled_on=&#8221;off|off|off&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; background_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; width=&#8221;100%&#8221; height=&#8221;175px&#8221; custom_margin=&#8221;0px||||false|false&#8221; custom_padding=&#8221;0px||0px||false|false&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243; border_color_all=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; saved_tabs=&#8221;all&#8221; collapsed=&#8221;off&#8221;][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243;][et_pb_column type=&#8221;4_4&#8243; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243;][et_pb_menu menu_id=&#8221;4&#8243; active_link_color=&#8221;#8300e9&#8243; dropdown_menu_line_color=&#8221;#0c71c3&#8243; dropdown_menu_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; dropdown_menu_active_link_color=&#8221;#8300e9&#8243; mobile_menu_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; logo_url=&#8221;\/home\/&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; menu_font=&#8221;|700|||||||&#8221; menu_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; menu_font_size=&#8221;15px&#8221; hover_enabled=&#8221;0&#8243;][\/et_pb_menu][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][et_pb_row _builder_version=&#8221;4.0.11&#8243; width=&#8221;100%&#8221; [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":3,"featured_media":0,"parent":33,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"page-template-blank.php","meta":{"_et_pb_use_builder":"on","_et_pb_old_content":"<p><strong>WPV is currently in search of a dynamic leader to join our team as the Executive Director.<\/strong> Westside Pacific Villages (WPV) is a grassroots, membership-based, and volunteer-driven non-profit that organizes a variety of connections, support, and events\u2013empowering people to better navigate the changes and opportunities that come with living longer. WPV helps older adults remain active and independent in the comfort and security of their own homes and neighborhoods. We do this with compassion, dignity, and respect.<\/p><p><strong>EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR POSITION DESCRIPTION<\/strong><br \/>The Executive Director (ED), working closely with the WPV Board of Directors (BOD), will be responsible for the leadership, development, and operations of the organization. This includes oversight of fundraising, client membership and volunteer recruitment, new program development and strategic and financial planning. The job requires working with a wide range of community organizations and people in addition to state organizations and institutions, and supervision of a small staff. This position is accountable to the WPV BOD on all matters.<\/p><p><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES<\/strong><br \/>Operations:<br \/>\u2022 Develop and maintain strategic and tactical plans for WPV with the guidance of the BOD<br \/>\u2022 Work with the staff, members, and volunteers to evaluate and enhance member benefits and services<br \/>\u2022 Prepare an annual budget for the organization with quarterly reviews with the BOD<br \/>\u2022 Maintain an efficient and organized business office compliant with necessary regulations.<br \/>\u2022 Recruit, manage, and develop staff, contractors, interns, and volunteers.<br \/>\u2022 Ensure Assisted Rides (CRM software) is accurate and up to date with WPV member and other information<br \/>\u2022 Responsible for contract management including negotiating and researching agreement terms<br \/>\u2022 Provide timely reports to the BDD on the health and the status of the organization<\/p><p><strong>Development\/Fundraising<\/strong><br \/>\u2022 Responsible for development and leading the fundraising plan for WPV<br \/>\u2022 Working closely with the BDD, identify and cultivate individuals, businesses, and philanthropic opportunities for funding<br \/>\u2022 Manage the development of donor solicitation materials<br \/>\u2022 Maintain existing and cultivate new development partnerships and opportunities<br \/>\u2022 Assist in the organization of special events, including donor\/volunteer appreciation events and other fundraising initiatives<br \/>\u2022 Assist in identifying grant opportunities, managing the grant development and proposal process<br \/>\u2022 Maintain security and quality controls of donor information and contributions.<\/p><p><strong>Member Services<\/strong><br \/>\u2022 With the support of the WPV BOD, recruits new client members and retains client membership renewals<br \/>\u2022 With support of the WPV BOD, recruits new volunteer members and retains adequate volunteer base to support client service requests.<br \/>\u2022 Deliver outstanding services and programming to WPV client and volunteer members<br \/>\u2022 Manage resources and supervise staff effectively to ensure excellent service is delivered to members<br \/>Community Outreach<br \/>\u2022 Maintain a calendar of outreach activities, including community events, workshops, appearances, and other communication opportunities<br \/>\u2022 Nurture new and old relationships with collaborative partners<br \/>\u2022 Schedule regular outreach opportunities in the community and engage BOD to participate<br \/>\u2022 Identify and establish an on-going relationship with surrounding community members and leaders<\/p><p><strong>QUALIFICATIONS<\/strong><br \/>\u2022 Proven senior level management experience with responsibility for multiple functional areas<br \/>\u2022 Prior experience working in a non-profit and working with a Board of Directors<br \/>\u2022 Self-directed and flexible, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously<br \/>\u2022 Outstanding organizational and time management skills, with attention to details and deadlines<br \/>\u2022 Strong written and verbal communication skills<br \/>\u2022 Experience working with elders, social service or in a health care environment<br \/>\u2022 Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite of products<br \/>\u2022 Ability to develop and manage budgets and prepare financial reports<br \/>\u2022 Must be comfortable presenting WPV\u2019s vision to a wide array of audiences\/groups<br \/>\u2022 Must be up to date on all vaccinations including COVID<\/p><p><strong>HOW TO APPLY<\/strong><br \/>Please submit your cover letter, resume, and salary requirements to <a href=\"mailto:careers@thewpv.org\">careers@thewpv.org<\/a> Only those whose applications are being considered will be contacted. No phone calls will be accepted.<br \/>Westside Pacific Villages is an equal opportunity employer.<\/p><p>\u00a0<\/p>"},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/2736"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/3"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2736"}],"version-history":[{"count":20,"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/2736\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":3283,"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/2736\/revisions\/3283"}],"up":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/33"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/thewpv.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2736"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}